WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.534
This morning, a popular energy

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.869
drink is under scrutiny.

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.471
Prime is a beverage

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:07.173
brand founded by YouTube stars Logan Paul

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:08.975
and KFC

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:09.809
Prime Energy

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.411
is especially popular with kids,

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:12.812
even though there is a warning label

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.314
that says it is not recommended

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:16.683
for anyone under age 18.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.817
Senator Chuck Schumer

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:18.118
is now

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:19.919
calling on the FDA to investigate

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.888
the drink over its high caffeine

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.957
and the way it markets itself.

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:25.025
I have

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.160
a lot of parents may never heard of it,

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.628
but their kids have

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:29.462
because crime

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.063
is engaged

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:30.630
in a vast

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.366
advertising campaign aimed at kids.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:35.502
Even though kids aren't supposed to drink

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:39.239
or drink with this much caffeine,

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.341
CNN has reached out to the FDA and prime

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.043
for comment on its energy drink.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.411
Not yet received a response.

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:45.211
We should note the company

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.280
also makes a prime hydrate beverage,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.115
which does not include caffeine

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:49.482
Joining us

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.283
now is CNN medical

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.384
correspondent Meg Terrell

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:52.352
and CNN business

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:53.620
and politics correspondent.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.388
Vanessa, your quick break

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.523
overserved with you.

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:57.590
The Senate majority leader saying

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.224
kids shouldn't

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.927
drink the amount of caffeine in prime.

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:03.063
How much caffeine does this drink have

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.031
and how much is safe for kids to consume?

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:05.298
Yeah,

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:05.932
so this

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:06.633
drink has about

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.368
200 milligrams of caffeine.

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:09.736
In a 12 ounce can.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:12.005
And to try to put that into some context,

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:14.407
that's about two bottles of Red Bull.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.008
Those are smaller

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.709
bottles, about 8.4 ounces

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.211
in a Red Bull can.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.580
Or about six cans of Coke.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.982
So that's in one of these cans.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:25.018
And according to the American Academy

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.352
of Pediatrics, really, kids

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.521
shouldn't have any caffeine

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.256
Some pediatricians say for kids

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:31.991
who are 12 and older,

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.893
maybe up to 100 milligrams per day,

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.129
that's a soda or two for adults.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:38.231
The FDA usually says about 400 milligrams

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.133
per day generally doesn't affect people.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.935
But for kids, the warnings are,

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.203
you know, this can affect their sleep.

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:43.670
It can cause

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:44.871
dehydration, higher

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.806
blood pressure, anxiety.

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:47.907
And there are concerns about

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.375
too much caffeine's impact

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.310
on their development

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.212
in terms of neurological development

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:54.447
in their cardiovascular systems, guys.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.548
And you see Chuck Schumer really

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.117
taking aim at the marketing here.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.284
So, Vanessa, on that note,

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:58.952
how is prime

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.320
cornering the market

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.355
and getting the attention of kids?

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:03.490
Well, primarily

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.958
exploited on social media.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:05.959
On TikTok alone,

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:08.528
they have 3.4 million followers.

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:11.231
42 million likes.

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:13.233
This is also driven in part by Logan

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.467
Paul, the co-founder

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:17.303
who has millions of followers himself.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.472
He does a lot of the advertising

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.673
for the brand.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:21.741
But it's important to note

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.643
that this is the energy drink

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:24.777
side of the brand.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.946
There's also the sports drink side.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.715
But the energy market is huge.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.216
In 20, 22

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:33.820
alone, sales were at about $58 billion,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.189
billion dollars this year.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:36.689
We're going to see

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:39.259
about $62 billion globally

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:41.661
and projected in the next four years.

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.363
$83 billion.

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:45.331
And most of those sales are happening

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.367
right here in North America.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.168
Another way

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.469
that this brand has gotten

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.237
sort of their face on the map

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.939
is they're sponsoring sports

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.707
teams, they're sponsoring the L.A.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.110
Dodgers, they're sponsoring Arsenal,

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.345
the soccer club Barcelona,

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.980
also based sports group,

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.949
which is a sponsorship group

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.884
for youth sports.

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.319
They are in good company

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:09.189
you have Adidas also sponsoring Arsenal.

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:10.723
You have Nike and Coca-Cola

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.525
sponsoring Barcelona.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:13.326
So clearly,

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:14.928
they are trying to make a play

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:16.262
and get their name out there.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.264
And it seems to be working, guys.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:19.165
Yeah, it's not subtle.

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.066
I'm slightly confused

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:20.967
how you consume the AR.

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:21.267
You drink

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.135
because all the promos

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.102
have them like pouring it on

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:23.803
their their heads

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:27.273
On a serious note, some

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.474
of the prime products say it's, quote,

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.510
not recommended for children under 18.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.212
If you're the FDA and you're

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:33.680
you do actually take a look at this.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.181
Is that enough?

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:36.115
Well, it really depends.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.684
I think from the FDA perspective,

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.052
from what I've been hearing from experts

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:39.552
this morning

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.087
on whether they are hearing

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:42.855
about instances of actual harm

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:43.590
coming from this.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:44.424
I was talking with former

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:46.326
FDA commissioner Dr. Scott Gottlieb.

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:48.361
He pointed out when he was in the role,

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:48.828
you know,

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:49.495
he issued

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:50.964
public health advisories

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:51.931
around things like this.

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:52.465
So that's just

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.667
to let people know about the situation

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.402
basically put out a warning

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.337
and some information

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:58.972
so that parents know about this.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.740
That is sort of a softer way of

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.275
of getting at the issue

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:03.209
than actually taking

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:03.676
any kind

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:04.744
of enforcement action,

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:05.712
which I'm hearing from experts,

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:07.614
is a much harder thing for the FDA

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:08.314
to do here.

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:09.782
But really, it's, you know,

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.384
is this actually causing harm?

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:12.552
And the marketing,

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:13.286
the nature of it

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.487
is that it specifically

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:16.923
bringing more children into the product?

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:17.590
Yeah, it's becoming

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.224
quite the status

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:19.926
symbol among children, right.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.427
To have these drinks in hand.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.096
It's no longer the shoes or whatever,

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:23.730
you know, kids.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.798
Popular on kids. It's about the drink.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:26.432
So this is really

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.201
a fascinating conversation.

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:29.702
Thank you so much, Meg, Vanessa,

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:30.470
we appreciate it.

